{
	title: 'Usage refresh replaces windows and names them by span',
	spec: "A /status usage-endpoint refresh replaces the account's stored windows with the ones it returns, including when the reading moves to a newly learnt email: windows of an old plan disappear instead of lingering until their reset in /status and rotation. OpenAI endpoint windows are named by their length like header windows (18000 s 5h, 604800 s 7d, a free plan's 2592000 s 30d), the raw primary/secondary only when no length is given. Response headers still merge, since one response may carry a subset. Invariant: stored windows are the provider's latest complete answer. Test: a refresh omitting a cached window drops it; a 30-day window is named 30d.",
